# The field is read in every turn. In front of the loop the box is asked for its shape and whether the slot is filled, failing to the closed copy; the slot is read once, and what it gives is told apart as what a variable holds is. In the copy for byte arrays no turn reads the slot.
# RUN(WALK): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES(WALK): entries-of-bun
# WALK: = ShapeTest
# WALK: = IsSlotFilled {{*}}key="bytes"
# WALK: [[given]]: {{*}} = GetSlot {{*}}key="bytes"
# WALK: = TypeTest [[given]] testedType=Array<number>
# WALK: = TypeTest [[given]] testedType=Uint8Array
# WALK: = GetTypedArrayVector
# WALK-NEXT: Jump
# WALK: = GetTypedArrayElement {{*}}typedArrayType=2 {{*}}isInsideView
